ENGLISH

This source code is publicly VIEWABLE but is NOT free or open source
software.

YOU MAY:
  - read the code;
  - study it for personal, educational or research purposes;
  - quote portions of it in technical discussion, with attribution.

YOU MAY NOT, without the copyright holder's written permission:
  - use the code, in whole or in part, in any product or service, whether
    commercial or free of charge;
  - copy, modify, translate it or create derivative works from it;
  - redistribute it, republish it elsewhere or sublicense it;
  - use it to train machine learning models.

Forking within GitHub is permitted by the platform's Terms of Service solely
for the purposes set out in those terms, and does not grant any of the rights
withheld above.

The repository is public for a practical rather than ideological reason:
public repositories get unlimited GitHub Actions minutes, and this project
uses a good many of them to collect news. Making the code readable is the
price of that choice, not a waiver of rights over it.

The data collected and processed (news archive, sentiment scores, time
series) is NOT part of this repository and is not covered by this licence.

Usage enquiries: michelesantacaterina08@gmail.com

